WEBVTT

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.980
<i>GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.990
'Scuse me. Coming in.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:22.990
What?!

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.740
Taromaru-san, was it?
I've got a juicy proposition for you.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.290
<i>The world you see isn't all there is.</i>

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.130
<i>There are things you can't see.</i>

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:44.970
<i>See? In the darkness behind you...</i>

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>Slumbering in bed in the morning</i>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>asa wa nedoko de gu gu gu</i>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.290
<i>Ghosts don't have school</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.290
<i>obakenya gakkou mo</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.170
<i>Or tests or anything</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.170
<i>shiken mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.550
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.550
<i>minna de utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.770
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.770
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.640
<i>Sports festivals in the graveyard at night</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.640
<i>yoru wa hakaba de undoukai</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.650
<i>Ghosts don't die</i>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.650
<i>obake wa shinanai</i>

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.070
<i>Or get sick or anything</i>

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.070
<i>byouki mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.540
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.540
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.870
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.870
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.840
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.840
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:19.060
But, why bring all these cucumbers
to a brand-new building like this?

00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:24.150
Who knows? The company president
told me not to ask.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:25.230
Let's go.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:26.440
Oh, right...

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:27.360
Huh?

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.660
Stop! Don't get involved.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:53.260
CHAPTER 9

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:58.180
THE KAPPAS' WORK REFORM

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:04.610
These were all in the Yokai Mailbox?

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:07.650
Yeah. And this is just today's...

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:09.280
Let's see...

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:13.660
"The spark between my wife and I
has gone out. Is this because of a <i>yokai</i>?"

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.780
"My exam scores are bad."

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.620
"I've been having
post-urination dribblage."

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.290
Are they stupid?

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:25.090
I'm not sure about this
blaming everything on <i>yokai</i>.

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:26.880
'Scuse me. Coming in.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:30.970
Oh! Looks like they're already rolling in.
What a haul!

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:32.890
What does that mean?

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.050
Well...

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:36.430
Ta-daa!

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:39.560
I put up an ad on the web.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:39.560
YOKAI MAILBOX
ASK ANYTHING

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.600
So this is your doing!

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:44.230
We'll solve problems in a flash,
make a bunch of cash, and--

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:48.440
Fine. If Kitaro won't do it...

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:51.400
Hey, Sand Witch!

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:54.530
Oh? Who's this?

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:56.160
A guest.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:59.540
Hello. I'm Taromaru the Kappa.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:02.830
Sand Witch-san always
takes good care of me.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:04.790
Hmm. Does she now?

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:09.550
Yes. When you mix Sand Witch-san's sand
with them, cucumbers grow well.

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:14.550
The Kappa tribe live deep in the Tono
mountains eating cucumbers, don't they?

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:15.550
Yes!

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:20.020
Oh, that's right. Sand Witch-san, here.

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:21.680
Some cucumbers as thanks.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:24.440
Thank you.

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:26.650
Hah! The barter system, huh?

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:29.730
If you sold that sand to the Kappa,
you could make a huge profit.

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:33.950
There are things in this world
more valuable than money!

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:36.530
You mean cucumbers? Talk about shabby!

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.870
You can have this sand instead!

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:45.290
Man! Honestly, nobody has any greed.

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:46.830
Huh?

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:49.130
Hmm...

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:52.630
"My father is the president of
an IT company.

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:55.380
He's been so busy recently
he's never home.

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:58.680
He's working without time to sleep
and seems strange."

00:04:58.800 --> 00:04:59.810
Hey!

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:02.980
What are you standing around for?!
Get me a change of clothes!

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:04.020
Yes, yes.

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:06.600
I don't have time!

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:09.230
It's Sunday,
but, he's still going to work.

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:10.690
I'm heading out!

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:13.110
Honey, won't you at least eat with us?

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.650
I don't have time to eat!

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:20.080
I made a reservation to eat French food
at a five-star hotel next month, didn't I?

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:26.040
I don't care about French food...

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:29.080
Food at normal restaurants
tastes better...

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:30.960
Things look serious.

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:34.970
Dad used to be nicer...

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:37.430
That's definitely the work of a <i>yokai</i>.

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:38.300
Huh?

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:41.890
Your father is being haunted by
the <i>yokai</i>, Isogashi.

00:05:42.010 --> 00:05:43.430
The <i>yokai</i>, Isogashi?

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:45.230
Will you get rid of it?

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:46.390
Of course.

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:50.690
But in that case...
Shall we discuss your budget?

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:54.150
I see. The <i>yokai</i>, Isogashi...

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:59.820
When haunted by the <i>yokai</i>, Isogashi, one
is filled with excess vigor and energy

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:02.950
and they find that they can't sit still...

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:04.330
But, Dad.

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:05.200
Hm?

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:08.920
I haven't heard
any rumors about Isogashi recently...

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:12.090
What?! I did something to a human?

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:13.880
I'm being falsely accused!

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.300
This is the <i>yokai</i>, Isogashi?

00:06:20.390 --> 00:06:22.640
Yeah! You got a problem with that?!

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:26.640
You seem to have
a lot of spare time these days.

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:32.270
Sure, I used to have fun
haunting different humans.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:35.730
But, these days,
I don't even have to bother...

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:43.580
It's become a world where everyone's
working like crazy...

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:47.040
Have you haunted any humans recently?

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:50.500
It's been ten years since I last did.

00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:56.710
Well, perhaps in a world like this,

00:06:56.840 --> 00:07:01.720
there's no need for
a <i>yokai</i> like me anymore...

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:08.680
The Japanese kanji for "busy"
means "the death of one's heart."

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:13.400
Even without being haunted by Isogashi,
humans who have lost their hearts

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:19.650
forget about kindness and compassion
and just work until they die...

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:24.530
There you have it, Rat Man.

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:28.790
The man in that letter
is just a workaholic.

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:34.960
Like I'm gonna leave
a potential tasty profit alone.

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:37.500
We can't anymore!

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:40.090
Wait! Are you running out on me?!

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:43.340
Shut up! We can't work
for such a low salary!

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:44.470
What?!

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:46.310
Oh! What a coincidence.

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:50.430
This building...
That guy's company must be inside.

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:53.980
There are things in this world
worth more than money!

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:56.820
Don't you have any dreams or aspirations?!

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:58.730
You're one to talk!

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:01.150
Oh, hey! Wait!

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:05.570
Things worth more than money, huh?
Someone else mentioned that.

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:08.790
...more valuable than money!

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:10.910
Oh yeah. That time with the Kappa...

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:13.370
-Hey! You there!
-Huh?

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:14.080
Huh?!

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:15.630
Wanna work for me?

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:18.250
Wh-Wh-What?!

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:20.260
There's nothing to worry about!

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:23.590
Newcomers are welcome.
It's a casual, warm workplace!

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:26.260
Wait, I'm not into that sort of...

00:08:26.390 --> 00:08:28.640
Don't be so shy!

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:33.230
My high school classmate, Ogawa,
founded the Little River Corporation.

00:08:33.350 --> 00:08:38.650
My college mate, Onogi,
puts out bestseller after bestseller.

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:41.820
I can't get left behind!

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:43.200
Please!

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:45.450
Let's dream the dream together!

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:48.200
Oh!

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:53.460
In that case, I know of someone
who'll work for dirt cheap.

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:54.620
What?

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:00.300
Ya-hoo!

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:10.560
Your cucumbers really are yummy, Taromaru.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:13.350
We can't harvest a lot at once, though.

00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:15.690
That's what makes them good!

00:09:15.810 --> 00:09:21.610
Someday I'd like to feed you
tons of cucumbers, Jiromaru...

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:26.570
Here. Take this.

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:28.200
Thanks, Taromaru!

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:32.660
Hello.

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:37.290
You! I met you in the GeGeGe Forest...

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:40.000
That's right. I'm the BiBiBi no Rat Man.

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:44.300
Taromaru-san, was it?
I've got a juicy proposition for you.

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:46.220
A juicy proposition?!

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:50.550
Right, this is perfect.
Listen up, everyone!

00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:54.980
Do you wanna eat lots of these
tasty-looking cucumbers?!

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:56.770
We do!

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:05.610
That's right. Looking good.

00:10:05.740 --> 00:10:08.240
Looking good. Keep it up.

00:10:10.280 --> 00:10:13.830
It's time for the cucumbers you've
been waiting for! Three per person!

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:23.960
What do you think, Mr. President? Really
cuts down on labor costs, doesn't it?

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:27.300
After all, their wages are only
three cucumbers an hour!

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:31.220
Eight hours of labor only costs you 24!

00:10:31.350 --> 00:10:33.010
Indeed. It's magnificent!

00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:37.560
Who knew you could hire <i>yokai</i> as
employees in this labor shortage?

00:10:41.190 --> 00:10:42.400
Taromaru!

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:43.610
Hey, what's wrong?!

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:45.820
My plate... It's dry...

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:48.240
I feel weak...

00:10:48.360 --> 00:10:50.740
What? They have such a weakness?!

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:54.450
Well, they're Kappa after all...
But fear not!

00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:57.450
Ta-daa! Moisturizing gel!

00:10:57.870 --> 00:11:02.540
Rub this on your plate and it'll maintain
the moisture for 24 hours without water.

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:11.340
Woo-hoo! I feel strength rising!

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:17.060
KAPPA

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:21.560
KAPPA ALPHABET

00:11:19.690 --> 00:11:20.560
<i>-"Bottom's up!"
-"Let's do it!"</i>

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:21.560
<i>"Cheers!"</i>

00:11:21.690 --> 00:11:24.310
What? You're sold out of cucumbers?!

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:26.610
You were out yesterday, too!

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:30.070
<i>The nationwide cucumber shortage
is showing no sign of subsiding.</i>

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:30.070
WHY ONLY A CUCUMBER SHORTAGE?

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:31.950
ONE CUCUMBER PER PERSON

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:36.700
<i>The cause of the shortage remains unclear.
Experts believe someone is buying all...</i>

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:39.500
Let's go.

00:11:39.620 --> 00:11:40.620
Oh, right...

00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:41.670
Huh?

00:11:44.710 --> 00:11:47.250
Stop! Don't get involved.

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:55.220
You saw...

00:11:56.260 --> 00:11:57.930
We saw nothing!

00:11:58.060 --> 00:11:59.100
Don't worry.

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:00.770
We won't kill you...

00:12:01.230 --> 00:12:04.270
We're just gonna
remove your <i>shirikodama</i>...

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:17.030
We're wasting time.
Let's get back to work!

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:24.250
-Taromaru...
-Hm?

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:27.040
Is this right for us?

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:31.840
Sure, we can eat lots of cucumbers,
but living every day like this...

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:36.010
Yeah, life back home was laid back.

00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:41.230
But, at best we could only eat
about three cucumbers a day.

00:12:41.350 --> 00:12:46.860
Cucumbers are just a luxury.
We don't need to eat that much to survive.

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:52.240
Rather, the time to lazily swim
in the river or take naps is...

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:53.610
You two!

00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:58.490
What are you slacking off there for?
Get back to work!

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:05.330
Hey! What's wrong?!

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:08.920
My plate... It's dry...

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:11.210
Aren't you using the moisturizing gel?

00:13:11.340 --> 00:13:14.090
There are limits to moisturizing gel!

00:13:15.090 --> 00:13:18.680
Mr. President, we can't continue
in these working conditions!

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:19.720
What?

00:13:19.850 --> 00:13:21.180
Taromaru!

00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:24.890
I request that our working conditions
be improved!

00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:29.570
Will you provide us with a shower room
we can freely use 24 hours a day?

00:13:30.650 --> 00:13:31.940
I like it!

00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:36.610
You've got a sharp sense!
Come dream the dream with me!

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:40.780
You like them, Mr. President?

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:40.780
PRESIDENT'S OFFICE

00:13:40.910 --> 00:13:45.620
Yes! I want to keep increasing Kappa
employees and expand the business!

00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:46.960
Leave it to me!

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:50.710
However, from here, the management fee
per Kappa will be...

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:52.090
about this much.

00:13:52.210 --> 00:13:55.090
-No. I don't need you anymore.
-Huh?

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:58.050
From here, I'll negotiate
directly with the Kappa.

00:13:58.180 --> 00:14:02.930
W-W-W-Wait a minute!
What about my services so far?!

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:05.390
Huh?

00:14:10.110 --> 00:14:12.730
What's wrong, Rat Man?

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:20.070
Hey, Kitaro, this lethargic manner.
Is it possible that...

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:22.700
his <i>shirikodama</i> has been removed?

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:24.080
His <i>shirikodama</i>?

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:25.910
Was this a Kappa's doing, Dad?

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:30.580
Come to think of it,
maybe the national cucumber shortage is...

00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:35.090
That's refreshing!

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:40.090
You know, working this hard
for only three cucumbers an hour?

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:42.390
Let's negotiate better wages.

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:44.810
We could probably get
five cucumbers an hour.

00:14:44.930 --> 00:14:48.520
Could we rent out the sumo arena
so we can do some wrestling?

00:14:48.640 --> 00:14:51.020
Everyone! Don't be fooled!

00:14:51.150 --> 00:14:52.560
-Huh?
-Look at this!

00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:55.070
It's a convenience store want ad.

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:58.070
It pays at least
1,000 yen an hour at night!

00:14:58.530 --> 00:15:01.910
At 50 yen a cucumber, you could buy 20!

00:15:02.030 --> 00:15:03.160
20?!

00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:04.740
We've been...

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:07.290
getting exploited!

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:09.960
Wh-What is this, you guys?!

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:13.250
You've been cheating us
and forcing us to work!

00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:18.050
The law guarantees our weekly work hours
and minimum wage!

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:19.760
Then try and sue me.

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:22.470
Too bad, though.

00:15:22.760 --> 00:15:28.770
While laws of employment apply to humans,
they don't apply to Kappa.

00:15:29.310 --> 00:15:31.230
The same goes for your wages.

00:15:31.350 --> 00:15:35.150
Sure, working at a convenience store
will earn you enough for 20 cucumbers.

00:15:35.270 --> 00:15:39.990
But, do you think Kappa like you
can just work at a convenience store?

00:15:40.110 --> 00:15:41.490
Of course you can't.

00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:44.280
If you did, there'd be panic in the city!

00:15:44.410 --> 00:15:50.330
You've got no choice but to huddle in this
building, unseen by people, and work!

00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:51.920
In that case...

00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:56.420
We'll just have to make it a world
where Kappa

00:15:56.550 --> 00:15:58.130
-can work openly!
-What?!

00:15:59.260 --> 00:16:00.510
What are you doing?!

00:16:10.430 --> 00:16:11.440
Huh?

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:30.830
<i>Emergency! The metropolitan area
is being overrun</i>

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:34.710
<i>by a mysterious group
with plate-like things on their heads!</i>

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:36.670
<i>Even near here...</i>

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:42.170
PLEASE STAND BY

00:16:48.010 --> 00:16:50.600
Don't you think that's about enough?

00:16:53.100 --> 00:16:54.020
The humans--

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:03.570
Hey, Kitaro! Get a grip!

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:10.240
Dad... I don't feel like
doing this anymore.

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:12.910
O-Oh no...

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:16.290
How dare you do that to Kitaro!
I'll fight you!

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:19.130
We won't hold back
just because you're a girl!

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:22.630
We'll take your <i>shirikodama</i>!

00:17:23.470 --> 00:17:24.880
No!

00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:27.180
No!

00:17:27.300 --> 00:17:30.060
Freaks! Stay away!

00:17:30.640 --> 00:17:33.430
Wally Wall!

00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:38.190
W-Wally Wall...

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:40.520
That was close!

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:42.440
A-whoosh!

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:45.740
Try to take my <i>shirikodama</i> if ya can!

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:49.990
C'mon!
Ya can't tell where my butt is, can ya?

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:52.120
I see it! Right here!

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:56.000
Ya got me...

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:58.750
Falling Cotton...

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:02.800
Taromaru!

00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:04.420
Stop this!

00:18:04.550 --> 00:18:07.800
Remember the taste of cucumbers
made with my sand!

00:18:08.260 --> 00:18:10.180
Sand Witch-san...

00:18:10.850 --> 00:18:13.810
I don't want to have to remove
your <i>shirikodama</i>...

00:18:14.390 --> 00:18:15.850
Taromaru...

00:18:16.310 --> 00:18:18.940
So we'll remove it instead!

00:18:26.150 --> 00:18:27.070
Sand Witch!

00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:28.530
Catchick!

00:18:36.830 --> 00:18:40.500
Huh. Everyone's gone all lethargic.

00:18:40.830 --> 00:18:44.170
After all this time,
is it my turn to shine again?

00:18:44.300 --> 00:18:44.960
Oh?

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:47.130
Oh! Isogashi!

00:18:58.850 --> 00:19:00.480
Hey, Kitaro!

00:19:05.570 --> 00:19:06.690
Remote Controlled Geta!

00:19:08.570 --> 00:19:09.490
Hair Needles!

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:12.620
Spirit Hair Chanchanko!

00:19:15.830 --> 00:19:16.950
Kitaro!

00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:18.830
You saved us!

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:21.540
Taromaru!

00:19:23.170 --> 00:19:23.960
So fast!

00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:34.850
Stop it, Taromaru!

00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:38.890
Kitaro-san, please forgive my brother!

00:19:39.180 --> 00:19:41.440
Here's your <i>shirikodama</i> back!

00:19:49.990 --> 00:19:53.370
Taromaru, this world isn't for us.

00:19:53.660 --> 00:19:54.990
Let's go back home.

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:56.870
B-But...

00:19:57.490 --> 00:19:58.450
the cucumbers...

00:19:59.410 --> 00:20:00.750
Forget those!

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:06.420
The cucumbers you shared with me
were tastier than a million cucumbers!

00:20:20.350 --> 00:20:21.600
Jiromaru...

00:20:23.810 --> 00:20:25.230
Taromaru...

00:20:42.370 --> 00:20:43.960
Over already?!

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:48.750
And I was having such fun
for the first time in so long...

00:20:56.850 --> 00:20:59.140
This Hamburg steak is delicious!

00:20:59.260 --> 00:21:02.810
Really? Then you can have half of mine!

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:05.480
Yay! Hooray!

00:21:09.980 --> 00:21:11.940
Ya-hoo!

00:21:17.070 --> 00:21:20.700
I guess you only need the cucumbers
you're going to eat a day.

00:21:20.830 --> 00:21:21.750
Yup!

00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:25.370
Take half of mine.

00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:26.540
Thanks.

00:21:29.420 --> 00:21:33.130
I've finally realized
what true happiness is!

00:21:33.260 --> 00:21:36.130
We'll live the self-sufficient,
slow life in the country!

00:21:36.260 --> 00:21:40.310
Our always-together-as-a-family,
happy life awaits!

00:21:40.430 --> 00:21:43.430
I don't wanna live in
the country like this! I can't take it!

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:44.430
Huh?!

00:21:44.560 --> 00:21:46.650
Go do that on your own!

00:21:47.020 --> 00:21:48.150
Huh?!

00:21:48.270 --> 00:21:49.980
See you!

00:21:50.110 --> 00:21:53.030
H-Hey! W-Wait!

00:21:53.150 --> 00:21:56.070
I guess, working too much
or living the slow life...

00:21:56.200 --> 00:22:00.450
Rather than go to the extremes,
people should take things in moderation.

00:22:00.580 --> 00:22:04.330
Humans have it tough, huh, Dad?

00:22:06.210 --> 00:22:07.370
<i>Oeoeo</i>

00:22:06.210 --> 00:22:07.370
<i>oeoeo</i>

00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:08.750
<i>Oeoeo</i>

00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:08.750
<i>oeoeo</i>

00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:11.420
<i>Oeoeoeoeo</i>

00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:11.420
<i>oeoeoeoeo</i>

00:22:11.550 --> 00:22:16.430
<i>Perhaps the truth lies
In what you can't see</i>

00:22:11.550 --> 00:22:16.430
<i>mienaimono ni koso shinjitsu ga
arukamo nante</i>

00:22:16.550 --> 00:22:19.300
<i>Do you believe that?
If you close your eyes</i>

00:22:16.550 --> 00:22:19.300
<i>kimi wa shinjirukana? me wo tojireba</i>

00:22:19.430 --> 00:22:23.890
<i>A new story will begin</i>

00:22:19.430 --> 00:22:23.890
<i>hajimaruyo atarashii monogatari</i>

00:22:24.850 --> 00:22:30.150
<i>The really important things</i>

00:22:24.850 --> 00:22:30.150
<i>taisetsu na mono wa itsudatte</i>

00:22:30.270 --> 00:22:34.940
<i>Are always things you can't see</i>

00:22:30.270 --> 00:22:34.940
<i>me niwa mienai monosa</i>

00:22:35.070 --> 00:22:37.780
<i>Looking up to a nameless sky</i>

00:22:35.070 --> 00:22:37.780
<i>namae no nai sora wo miage</i>

00:22:37.910 --> 00:22:40.910
<i>I bittersweetly counted dreams</i>

00:22:37.910 --> 00:22:40.910
<i>hiki komogomo yume wo kazoeta</i>

00:22:41.030 --> 00:22:43.540
<i>Are you honest with yourself?</i>

00:22:41.030 --> 00:22:43.540
<i>kimi wa jibun ni shoujikikai?</i>

00:22:43.870 --> 00:22:48.460
<i>The wind tickled my nose</i>

00:22:43.870 --> 00:22:48.460
<i>kaze ga hana wo kusugutta</i>

00:22:48.830 --> 00:22:51.500
<i>Lost in the dark night, oeoeo</i>

00:22:48.830 --> 00:22:51.500
<i>yamiyo ni magirete oeoeo</i>

00:22:51.630 --> 00:22:54.250
<i>Oeoeo oeoeo</i>

00:22:51.630 --> 00:22:54.250
<i>oeoeo oeoeo</i>

00:22:54.380 --> 00:22:56.720
<i>From behind you, oeoeo</i>

00:22:54.380 --> 00:22:56.720
<i>kimi no ushiro kara oeoeo</i>

00:22:56.840 --> 00:23:01.640
<i>Oeoeo oeoe o o o</i>

00:22:56.840 --> 00:23:01.640
<i>oeoeo oeoe o o o</i>

00:23:06.140 --> 00:23:09.060
<i>Dad, it looks like the </i>yokai
<i>at Mana's school</i>

00:23:09.190 --> 00:23:11.520
<i>have gotten involved in some incident.</i>

00:23:11.940 --> 00:23:14.320
<i>Next time on GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:23:14.440 --> 00:23:16.940
<i>"Vanishing! The Seven School Mysteries"</i>

00:23:17.070 --> 00:23:19.660
<i>The door to the unseen world opens...</i>
